WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
In a Germany where pensioners have to collect pfand bottles to get around the roundabouts.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Where you stand at train stations and wait for your train to arrive, even if it has not already arrived.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Where you are tense every minute in the train station area, because you know that the attacks by the usual suspects are normal.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
A Germany in which child wars are not just a question of the heart, but above all a question of money.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Where Kitas are not only overcrowded, but where the people who care for our little ones are underpaid and overworked.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Where ministers sacrifice the economic future of a whole nation without consideration for jobs,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
affordable energy or the competitiveness of our country.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
In a Germany where clan wars and drug trade belong to everyday life in many parts of the city.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Where laws are being passed, but those that break them have no consequences to fear.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
But in this Germany we also see a chance. A chance for change.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.000
For a country that listens to its citizens again.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
For politicians who have to take responsibility if they lead our country into ruin.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.000
To have consequences for this and have to make a professional new start outside the Berlin political landscape.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
And it's time for re-immigration.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Migration. Migrants without a valid residence permit must be consistently and quickly brought back to their home countries.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Especially for migrants who have become criminal, there should be no tolerance.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.000
It is time to address the real problems of this country.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Time to focus on the people who live, work and preserve this country.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.000
It is time to act with reason.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
For an energy policy that guarantees stability instead of creating uncertainties.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000
It's time for a new beginning.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Time to make our country strong again.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Time for Germany.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.000
On February 23 with both voices.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
AfD
